/*
:name: absent_field_one_field_tuple
:type: error
:error: unknown field `zz`
*/
// Reading an absent field is a compile error (03-bundle.md; ruling 2026-09-28
// #24: a read with no accessible declaration is an error at the read, never
// nil). A tuple with 2+ fields always reported `unknown-field`, but one whose
// ONLY field is named was read as a scalar by upass.constprop's field read
// (the single-output callee fallback), so a DEAD read of an absent field
// compiled with exit 0 (a live one failed only indirectly, `upass.tolg:
// unresolved reference`). imports/absent_field_one_member_import.prp is the
// one-member import namespace twin; test-block instance handles
// (`mut d = dut; d.a = 3; d.o`) are a different thing and stay legal
// (sim/test_read_after_tick.prp, sim/test_bare_step_multi_input.prp).
pub comb absent_field_one_field_tuple(a:U8) -> (o:U8) {
  const t = (const x = a)
  const q = t.zz  // locate_error_here
  o = a
}
